# A model asked through the host's proxy (typed): virtio-net drives the
# card, on QEMU's user network, and inet is the stack. On the host,
# e2e.sh runs tools/api-proxy/e2e_serve.py (serve): the stand-in for the
# Messages API, answering from script.json, and the proxy in front of it
# on a free port, @PORT@, which agent/config names at 10.0.2.2; the
# proxy takes agent/token, this case's own, which only the stand-in's
# proxy knows. ask is run twice: to a stream of four text pieces,
# written as they come, and to a 529, whose overloaded error it says.
start /bin/sh
start /sbin/uart noecho
start /sbin/virtio-net
start /sbin/inet
dev /sbin/uart
dev /sbin/virtio-net
